From fcfe61ad8cb2c113bfc0d72f47ab1f6e204c9091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneshot <oneshot@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:40:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] 0064 android: universal fixes: Turnip only on Adreno, no zip
 handler, safe backup and restore

- ModImportActivity has no intent filters: OneShot (no mods on Android) is not in
  Open with / Share for every zip.
- The Turnip block, the first-run driver button and the Turnip tip only on
  Adreno GPUs; the first-run button opens Settings with More unfolded.
- Backup: none made without worlds; the old backup goes only once the new one
  is in place.
- Restore: the backup is copied before the worlds are moved aside; a failed
  copy leaves them where they were, and saves-replaced is kept until then.
- World import clears left-over .importing folders and checks canonical paths;
  the world being exported survives the process ending under the picker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
